{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgwKs7fPQ1XnoAcHMjVQH","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01KYu2b973U8xPqekt5Pb9df","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /workspace/paper; python3 - <<'E'\nt=open('paper.tex').read()\ndef rep(a,b):\n    global t\n    assert t.count(a)==1,a[:40]; t=t.replace(a,b)\nrep(r\"Prompt and pipeline optimizers such as DSPy and MIPRO search over instructions, demonstrations and multi-call structures on a benchmark sample \\citep{Khattab2023DSPy,OpsahlOng2024MIPRO}, and\",\n    r\"Prompt and pipeline optimizers such as DSPy and MIPRO search over instructions, demonstrations and multi-call structures on a benchmark sample \\citep{Khattab2023DSPy,OpsahlOng2024MIPRO}, LLM-driven optimizers propose and rank candidate prompts by their score on a task sample \\citep{Zhou2022APE,Yang2023OPRO}, and\")\nrep(r\"It is therefore a biased estimate of that candidate's accuracy on new questions, and the usual interval around it ignores the selection.\",\n    r\"It is therefore a biased estimate of that candidate's accuracy on new questions, and the usual interval around it ignores the selection. This is the selection bias long documented for model selection, where the score used to pick among many candidates is an optimistic performance estimate \\citep{Cawley2010Overfitting}.\")\nrep(r\"; \\citet{Hardt2014Hard} showed that preventing false discovery in fully interactive analysis is computationally hard, and \\citet{Ullman2017TechnicalPB,Dwork2017GuiltfreeDR} give overviews.\",\n    r\"; and \\citet{Hardt2014Hard} showed that preventing false discovery in fully interactive analysis is computationally hard.\")\nrep(r\"and \\citet{Marchant2024AdaptiveDA} extended the setting to growing data; \", r\"\")\nrep(r\"Benchmark overfitting under repeated reuse has been probed on image classification by collecting a fresh test set \\citep{Recht2019ImageNet}.\",\n    r\"In machine learning, the optimism of a score used to choose among candidates is a documented source of selection bias in model selection \\citep{Cawley2010Overfitting}, and benchmark overfitting under repeated reuse has been probed empirically, on image classification by collecting a fresh test set \\citep{Recht2019ImageNet} and by studying how the number of classes affects overfitting from test-set reuse \\citep{Feldman2019MultipleClasses}. We study the same optimism for searched LLM configurations, with ground truth supplied by the evaluator.\")\nrep(r\"DSPy \\citep{Khattab2023DSPy} and MIPRO \\citep{OpsahlOng2024MIPRO} automate prompt and pipeline optimization, best-arm\",\n    r\"DSPy \\citep{Khattab2023DSPy} and MIPRO \\citep{OpsahlOng2024MIPRO} automate prompt and pipeline optimization, LLM-driven optimizers generate and select instructions by their score on task examples \\citep{Zhou2022APE,Yang2023OPRO}, best-arm\")\nrep(r\"multi-prompt evaluation can be made sample-efficient \\citep{Polo2024EfficientMultiPrompt}, and\",\n    r\"multi-prompt evaluation can be made sample-efficient \\citep{Polo2024EfficientMultiPrompt}, item response theory has been used to analyse machine-learning classifiers at the instance level \\citep{MartinezPlumed2019IRTinAI}, and\")\nrep(r\"where $a_k$ is a configuration effect, $b_q$ a question difficulty\",\n    r\"a Rasch-type item response model with hierarchical priors, whose item parameters are classically estimated by marginal maximum likelihood with EM \\citep{Bock1981MML}; our fit below instead alternates Newton sweeps over configuration and question parameters with Laplace-corrected variance updates. Here $a_k$ is a configuration effect, $b_q$ a question difficulty\")\nopen('paper.tex','w').write(t)\nE\nsed -n 99,106p paper.tex | cut -c1-400"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2470,"cache_read_input_tokens":63495,"cache